<h2 class="bold" id="accessibility"><a class="underline reset-text-decoration" href="modal#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
<ul>
<li>Modals should only be opened by activating a <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">button</span></span></code></span> element.</li>
<li>Opening a modal sets focus on element with <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">data-a11y-modal-initial-focus</span></span></code></span>
attribute (modal title by default). When not present, focus is set on first
focusable element, usually the close button.</li>
<li>An open modal traps focus. It must always contain a close button.</li>
<li>Pressing ESC or clicking the overlay closes the modal.</li>
<li>Closing a modal sets focus back on the activating <span class="code-wrapper code-container inline" style="background-color:hsl(230, 1%, 98%);color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><code class="code code--inline prism-code language-markup code-inline"><span class="token-line" style="color:hsl(230, 8%, 24%)"><span class="token plain">button</span></span></code></span> element.</li>
</ul>
